                <pb facs="0779" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1177</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-06T11:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 6, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                    </date> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8:30 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Referring to my cable of November 4, 5 p.m., the Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    informed me Norwegian Government has sent a protest to the British Government
                    against closing of the North Sea. Denmark and Sweden will do same. Norway
                    depends on the United States for large amount of supplies. The Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs expressed a hope that they will have the support of the United
                    States and the United States Government will protest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
